{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, קֳדָם","hw":"קֳדָם","html":"<big><span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָם</span></big><sub>42</sub>  <strong>prep. before (</strong>so Old Aramaic Nab. Palm. etc. (Lzb<sup>360 f.</sup>), 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">קָדָם</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܩܕܳܡ</span>; proposes a subst. <em>the front</em>, cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">قُدَّام</span> <em>the front;</em> for √ v. BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, קדם\" href=\"/BDB,_קדם\", dir=\"rtl\">קדם</a><strong>)</strong>;—sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָמַי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:9\" href=\"/Daniel.2.9\">Dn 2:9</a> +, -<span dir=\"rtl\">מָ֑י</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:6\" href=\"/Daniel.2.6\">6</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קדמיך</span> Kt, <span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָמָךְ</span> Qr, †<a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:23\" href=\"/Daniel.5.23\">5:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:23\" href=\"/Daniel.6.23\">6:23</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָמוֹהִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:5\" href=\"/Daniel.4.5\">4:5</a> + (cf. Nerab <span dir=\"rtl\">קדמוה</span>, Cooke<sup>189</sup>); 3 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">קדמיה</span> Kt, <span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָמַהּ</span> Qr, †<a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:7\" href=\"/Daniel.7.7\">7:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:8\" href=\"/Daniel.7.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:20\" href=\"/Daniel.7.20\">20</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קֳדָמֵיהוֹן</span> †<a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:4\" href=\"/Daniel.4.4\">4:4</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>before</em> (= Heb. <span dir=\"rtl\">לִפְנֵי</span>), especially in the phrases <em>to answer, pray, say</em> etc., <em>before</em> a superior (as more respectful than <em>to</em>), <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:9\" href=\"/Daniel.2.9\">Dn 2:9</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לְמֵאמַר קֳדָמַי</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:10\" href=\"/Daniel.2.10\">10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:11\" href=\"/Daniel.2.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:27\" href=\"/Daniel.2.27\">27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:11\" href=\"/Daniel.6.11\">6:11</a> (v. Dr), v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:12\" href=\"/Daniel.6.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:13\" href=\"/Daniel.6.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:14\" href=\"/Daniel.6.14\">14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קֱרִי ק׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:18\" href=\"/Ezra.4.18\">Ezr 4:18</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:23\" href=\"/Ezra.4.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:23\" href=\"/Daniel.5.23\">5:23</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; with <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׁפַר</span> to <em>seem fair</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:32\" href=\"/Daniel.3.32\">Dn 3:32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:2\" href=\"/Daniel.6.2\">6:2</a>; after vbs. of motion, <em>in before</em>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:24\" href=\"/Daniel.2.24\">Dn 2:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:25\" href=\"/Daniel.2.25\">25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:13\" href=\"/Daniel.3.13\">3:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:3\" href=\"/Daniel.4.3\">4:3</a> +; of time <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:7\" href=\"/Daniel.7.7\">7:7</a>.<br>†<strong>2.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן־קֳדָם</span> <em>from before</em> (= <span dir=\"rtl\">מִלִּפְנֵי</span>, but as used in <em>late</em> Heb., <a data-ref=\"Esther 1:19\" href=\"/Esther.1.19\">Est 1:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Esther 4:8\" href=\"/Esther.4.8\">4:8</a>: p. 818<sup>a</sup>), c. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַבֵּל</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:6\" href=\"/Daniel.2.6\">Dn 2:6</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּעָא</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:18\" href=\"/Daniel.2.18\">18</a>; of a decree, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:27\" href=\"/Daniel.6.27\">6:27</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן־קֳדָמַי שִׂים טְעֵם</span> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:18\" href=\"/Daniel.3.18\">3:29</a> +), cf <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:15\" href=\"/Daniel.2.15\">2:15</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:14\" href=\"/Ezra.7.14\">Ezr 7:14</a>; of God, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:24\" href=\"/Daniel.5.24\">Dn 5:24</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן־קֳדָמוֹהִי שְׁלִיחַ פַּסָּא דִּי־יְדָא</span>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:10\" href=\"/Daniel.7.10\">7:10</a> (so very often in 𝔗, Dr<sup>Sm lxx. f., lxxiii</sup>). Also = Heb. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִפְּנֵי</span>, with to <em>fear</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:19\" href=\"/Daniel.5.19\">Dn 5:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:27\" href=\"/Daniel.6.27\">6:27</a>, be <em>rooted up</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:8\" href=\"/Daniel.7.8\">7:8</a> <em>fall</em> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:20\" href=\"/Daniel.7.20\">20</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, קַדְמָה","prev":"BDB Aramaic, קַבֵּל"}